From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andriy Chuma <chuma.andriy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:35:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] m68k: flippies: Add the framebuffer and PS/2 port drivers

Add drivers for the displays and the PS/2 ports of the Create Flippies
PC, for the platform devices that arch/m68k/flippies registers.

flippiesfb drives each of the three displays as an fbdev device. A
display has a control window and 512 KiB of video memory of its own;
the driver uses its 8-bit pseudocolour modes, 640x480 (the default) and
320x200, with the palette at 0x400 in the control window. The display
shows video memory from a byte offset, so the virtual screen is as tall
as video memory allows and panning moves that offset. The video memory
is mapped by fb_io_mmap. FBIO_WAITFORVSYNC waits for the display's
vertical blank interrupt, which is enabled only while a task waits, and
FBIOGET_VBLANK reports the frame counter. fbcon runs on fb0.

flippies_ps2 drives each PS/2 port as a serio port. The controller
passes the bytes of the device unchanged, so each port registers as
SERIO_8042 with a write callback: atkbd then stays raw in scancode set
2, and psmouse binds when a mouse is plugged in instead.

Each port's interrupt stays enabled from probe on, as i8042's do, so a
byte from a device plugged into a port with no driver bound makes serio
rescan the port: a keyboard or mouse plugged in after boot binds.
